{
  "_comment": "Per-project Claude Code settings written by /ar-install. AUTONOMOUS posture: the agentic flow (ar-taskflow and friends) runs end to end without permission prompts. 'allow' is broad and STACK-NEUTRAL on purpose, never pruned per project, so a repo that gains a second language does not start prompting. 'ask' holds only the operator decisions where a human's answer in the moment changes the outcome (merging a PR, deleting a branch or volume); none of them sits on the normal flow, so the flow still never blocks. 'deny' holds only what must never run. SAFETY DOES NOT LIVE HERE: a permission entry is a prefix match, so it cannot stop `bash -c` or a rephrased command. Default-branch commits, force pushes, shared-branch history rewrites, whole-tree discards, `git reset --hard` and `git clean` are refused by the PreToolUse guard that install.sh wires globally (scripts/ar-session/guard-default-branch.sh), which is why `git` and `gh` can be allowed wholesale here. The authoritative control is server-side branch protection.",
